 "Cross Country Skiing"] "\n" [:option {:value "CUR"} "Curling"] "\n" [:option {:value "FSK"} "Figure Skating"] "\n" [:option {:value "FRS"} "Freestyle Skiing"] "\n" [:option {:value "IHO"} "Ice Hockey"] "\n" [:option {:value "LUG"} "Luge"] "\n" [:option {:value "NCB"} "Nordic Combined"] "\n" [:option {:value "STK"} "Short Track Speed Skating"] "\n" [:option {:value "SKN"} "Skeleton"] "\n" [:option {:value "SJP"} "Ski Jumping"] "\n" [:option {:value "SBD"} "Snowboarding"] "\n" [:option {:value "SSK"} "Speed Skating"]]] [:script {} "$('#sports_in_same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/62/sports/'+$('#sports_in_same_games_select').val()})"] [:form {:id "other_games_form", :class "form-inline", :style "display: inline", :method "get"} [:select {:name "year", :id "sport_in_other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "Biathlon in other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "36"} "1960 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "37"} "1964 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "38"} "1968 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "39"} "1972 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "40"} "1976 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "41"} "1980 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "42"} "1984 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "43"} "1988 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "44"} "1992 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "45"} "1994 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "46"} "1998 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "47"} "2002 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "49"} "2006 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "57"} "2010 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "66"} "2012 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "58"} "2014 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "68"} "2016 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "60"} "2018 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "70"} "2020 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "73"} "2024 Winter Youth Olympics"] "\n" [:option {:value "72"} "2026 Winter Olympics"]]] [:script {} "$('#sport_in_other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/editions/' + $('#sport_in_other_games_select').val() + '/sports/BTH'})"] "\n" [:h1 {} "Biathlon at the 2022 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:table {:class "biodata"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Dates"] "\n" [:td {} "5 – 18 February 2022"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal Events"] "\n" [:td {} "11"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Venues"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/2138"} "Zhangjiakou Nordic Centre and Biathlon Centre, Chongli District, Zhangjiakou City, Hebei Province"]] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "Biathlon summary"] "\n\n" [:p {} "The biathlon program did not change from the last two Winter Games, after the introduction of the mixed relay at Sochi in 2014. The results of the Olympic competitions did not count towards the World Cup for the 2021/22 season."] "\n\n" [:p {} "All events took place at the Zhangjiakou National Biathlon Centre located 180 km north-west of Beijing, in Hebei province. Most took place in the late afternoon under a lighted course. As has been common in recent years, the longest individual events, the traditional 20 km for men and 15 km for women, were held by adding 1-minute penalties for missed targets, while the penalty in all the other events was skiing an additional 150-metre penalty loop for each missed shot."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Weather conditions varied, particularly for the mixed relay, the very first event, and the concluding mass starts, which were influenced by variable icy winds and extreme cold of more than -15° C. The women’s mass start, scheduled to be the last event on February 19th, was brought forward by one day to avoid even worse conditions."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Several 2018 Olympic Winter Games gold medal winners had retired, including individual gold medalists " [:a {:href "/athletes/118554"} "Martin Fourcade"] " (3 golds), " [:a {:href "/athletes/127804"} "Laura Dahlmeier"] " (2), " [:a {:href "/athletes/118509"} "Arnd Peiffer"] ", and " [:a {:href "/athletes/118501"} "Anastasia Kuzmina"] " (1 each). " [:a {:href "/athletes/84154"} "Ole Einar Bjørndalen"] ", the most successful Winter Olympian ever, and his wife " [:a {:href "/athletes/118516"} "Daria Domrachava"] ", had also retired from active sport and had the task of preparing the inexperienced Chinese team for their home Olympics."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Three athletes dominated the events with five medals each: Norwegian " [:a {:href "/athletes/128188"} "Johannes Thingnes Bø"] " (4G – 1B), Frenchman " [:a {:href "/athletes/137167"} "Quentin Fillon Maillet"] " (2G – 3S), and among the females, " [:a {:href "/athletes/137711"} "Marte Olsbu Røiseland"] " (3G – 2B). The only individual gold medals that were claimed by other athletes came in the women’s individual, (" [:a {:href "/athletes/127819"} "Denise Herrmann"] "), and mass start (" [:a {:href "/athletes/137165"} "Justine Braisaz-Bouchet"] ")."] "\n\n" [:p {} "By far the most medals, including six gold, went to Norway (14), who won more than half of the eleven events. Brothers " [:a {:href "/athletes/128188"} "Johannes Thingnes"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/118590"} "Tarjei Bø"] " were members of the victorious men’s and mixed relay teams. With two individual medals, Tarjei Bø and " [:a {:href "/athletes/128184"} "Tiril Eckhoff"] " also contributed to Norway’s medal haul."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Second in the medal table was France, with three golds (as in 2018) and four silver, with additional silver by " [:a {:href "/athletes/127715"} "Anais Chevalier-Bouchet"] " in the women’s individual. Sweden benefitted from their strong women’s team taking gold in the relay and two individual silver by " [:a {:href "/athletes/148988"} "Elvira Öberg"] ". The only medal for Sweden’s men’s team was won by " [:a {:href "/athletes/138153"} "Martin Ponsiluoma"] " in the last event, the mass start."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In PyeongChang in 2018, Germany were the biathlon medal table leaders, but disappointed in Beijing with only Herrmann’s gold, and a bronze in women’s relay, being their complete haul. Their men’s team left empty-handed for the first time since 2010. The Russian biathletes competed in full strength as Russian Olympic Committee (ROC), winning medals (1S – 2B) in the three relays. Their only individual medal was won by " [:a {:href "/athletes/148769"} "Eduard Latypov"] " in the men’s pursuit. The same athlete became somewhat of a tragic figure losing gold in the men’s relay at the last shooting."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Former World Cup winner " [:a {:href "/athletes/127919"} "Dorothea Wierer"] " claimed her first individual medal in the women’s sprint at her third Olympic Winter Games. Surprisingly, " [:a {:href "/athletes/136770"} "Anton Smolski"] " collected the only medal for Belarus after flawless shooting in the individual. The country’s higher rated women never came closer to a medal, with " [:a {:href "/athletes/147892"} "Hanna Sola"] "’s fourth place finish in the pursuit being their best result."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/19019630"} "10 kilometres Sprint, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "12 February 2022"] "\n" [:td {} "94"] "\n" [:td {} "28"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/19019631"} "12.5 kilometres Pursuit, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "13 February 2022"] "\n" [:td {} "59"] "\n" [:td {} "22"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/19019632"} "15 kilometres Mass Start, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "18 February 2022"] "\n" [:td {} "30"] "\n" [:td {} "13"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/19019633"} "20 kilometres, Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} " 8 F